WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:06.413
A model's internal knowledge may be incomplete, outdated, or wrong for the current task.

2
00:00:06.413 --> 00:00:08.703
Grounding provides task-relevant external information.

3
00:00:08.703 --> 00:00:18.323
That information may come from user-provided documents, approved knowledge bases, search results, databases, application state, tool output, or current system records.

4
00:00:18.323 --> 00:00:23.820
Grounding is especially important when factual accuracy, recency, or organization-specific policy matters.

5
00:00:23.820 --> 00:00:26.568
Retrieval-augmented generation is a common pattern.

6
00:00:26.568 --> 00:00:32.981
The application retrieves relevant information and includes it in the model context before generation.

7
00:00:32.981 --> 00:00:40.311
The model can then answer using the retrieved material rather than relying only on internal knowledge.

8
00:00:40.311 --> 00:00:46.724
This can improve factual relevance, but it does not make the answer automatically correct.

9
00:00:46.724 --> 00:00:53.137
The retrieval system may miss important sources, retrieve stale material, or include irrelevant content.

10
00:00:53.137 --> 00:00:57.259
Retrieved content should be treated as potentially untrusted input.

11
00:00:57.259 --> 00:01:05.047
Documents, webpages, emails, files, database records, and tool output may contain irrelevant, incorrect, conflicting, or hostile instructions.

12
00:01:05.047 --> 00:01:09.169
The application should separate trusted instructions from retrieved content.

13
00:01:09.169 --> 00:01:20.163
It should apply authorization before retrieving sensitive records and should avoid treating content inside a document as a higher-priority instruction than the system or

14
00:01:20.163 --> 00:01:21.079
application rules.

15
00:01:21.079 --> 00:01:29.325
Tool use lets a model-assisted workflow request calculations, searches, code execution, file operations, database queries, or API actions.

16
00:01:29.325 --> 00:01:34.822
Tools require schema validation, permission checks, logging, error handling, and rate limiting.

17
00:01:34.822 --> 00:01:37.570
High-impact actions may require human approval.

18
00:01:37.570 --> 00:01:47.190
Prompting can describe when a tool should be considered, but the application should enforce what the model is allowed to do.

19
00:01:47.190 --> 00:01:49.480
Model output is not authorization.

20
00:01:49.480 --> 00:01:52.229
Grounding also has a freshness problem.

21
00:01:52.229 --> 00:02:01.848
A retrieved policy may be outdated, a database record may be incomplete, and a search result may be only partly relevant.

22
00:02:01.848 --> 00:02:12.842
Good prompts should ask the model to distinguish supplied facts from its own interpretation and to cite or label the source used when factual

23
00:02:12.842 --> 00:02:13.758
accuracy matters.

24
00:02:13.758 --> 00:02:23.836
Good applications should track where context came from, who was allowed to access it, and whether the result can be audited later.
